{"id": "9e0d56d4-0c7b-438d-ba36-7c58a4009fdf", "role": "assistant", "content": [{"thinking": "The instance is stopped now — it's a c6i.xlarge, which is EBS-optimized by default so that attribute reading odd isn't a concern. I need to pull instance type details, EBS volume status for all five volumes, and metrics covering the incident window from 15:30 to 15:47 against a 15:00 baseline.

I'm planning to query per-minute metrics from 15:00 to 16:00 for the specific volume covering reads, writes, bytes, latency, queue length, and idle time, plus aggregate ops and bytes across the other volumes, and also check EBSIOBalance% since the c6i.xlarge has burstable EBS throughput with a 1250 Mbps baseline and 10000 Mbps burst. I'll set this up using a metric math query across all these dimensions.

